Well, i ascended a wizard once who played as a water nymph for more
than half of the game. Final hitpoints in nymph shape were 250ish. You
_definitely_ want to play with unchanging on in such a case, because
the "fresh" form has something on the order of 15HP. 
Extra max hitpoints from potions of *healing, nurses and golden glows
will apply to the shapechanged form, not to the original
(human/gnomish/whatever) character's shape. Also, if you advance in
level while polymorphed, the polymorphed form will gain max hitpoints
(but no extra hitdice). All such gains are, of course, lost if you
turn back into your original shape and (control-)polymorph into a
monster again.

The low hitdice were mainly a problem because they made it hard for my
character to hit the fully-decked-out adventurers on Astral, even with
maxed luck and stats and an expertly wielded +3 Magicbane.

